 From: RAY DUNCAN                      Read: NO
 Subj: MEMORY AND PIC                Status: PUBLIC MESSAGE

 Dynamic memory allocation is very useful.  All of the LMI Forth systems
 have had this for several years.  But I agree that it should be viewed
 as an extension to the language rather than part of the core language
 (similar to its implementation as part of the RTL in C) --- it doesn't
 make any sense to require that this be supported in a ROM'd ANSI
 Standard FORTH kernel, for example.

 NET/Mail : LMI Forth Board, Los Angeles, CA (213) 306-3530             
