 Date: 06-16-90 (10:54)              Number: 652 (Echo)
   To: JEFF CYNX                     Refer#: NONE
 From: RAY DUNCAN                      Read: NO
 Subj: COMMENT                       Status: PUBLIC MESSAGE

 My injunction against this is both worldy and spiritual.  If you want
 your program to run properly under multitasking environments such as
 DesqView, Win 3, OS/2's DOS box, etc. you should be "well-behaved" in
 your use of memory.  Not using MALLOC means that you will not be able to
 use new capabilities such as SHELL" and that your program will not be
 easily portable to the higher-performance UR/FORTH systems for DOS,
 OS/2, or 32-bit 80386 protected mode.

 NET/Mail : LMI Forth Board, Los Angeles, CA (213) 306-3530             
